            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnosis of postpartum abdominal pain: about a rare case of portal vein thrombosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.gyobfe.2014.07.021</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1297-9589(14)00229-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the management of patient with acute abdominal pain in the immediate post-partum caesarean section performed in the context of preeclampsia. Acute portal vein thrombosis is diagnosed, in a patient with no personal or family history of venous thrombosis. Blood tests showed a protein C and S deficiencies. Portal vein thrombosis is an extremely rare occurrence in pregnancy and postpartum.</AbstractText>
